<title>BELGIUM: RENAULT WORKERS DEMO SET TO BLOCK BRUSSELS TRAFFIC.</title>
<headline>RENAULT WORKERS DEMO SET TO BLOCK BRUSSELS TRAFFIC.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A demonstration by 3,100 workers of Renault Belgium, protesting against the closure of their Vilvoorde plant, is set to disrupt traffic in the Brussels city centre on Monday.</p>
<p>The march is set to start mid-morning at the Jubelpark/Parc du Cinquantenaire. It will proceed through Wetstraat, rue Belliard and then move back to the starting point via the European Union quarter.</p>
<p>Renault announced the plant closure on Thursday. Renault workers and Belgian authorities have protested vehemently.</p>
<p>Belgian radio said that workers of bankrupt steel firm Clabecq were also set to join the march.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
